.playwright-mcp/
node_modules

# Runtime client data — contains plaintext passwords and KYC/PII.
# Never commit these; they live on the server only.
#
# Everything in these directories is ignored, not a list of filenames. The list
# was the whole protection, so a users.json.backup made before an experiment —
# exactly the thing a careful person does — was committable, and would have
# carried every password and KYC record with it. Only the deny rule is tracked.
data/*
!data/.htaccess
data.*/*
!data.*/.htaccess

# Uploaded identity documents. The directory and its deny rule are tracked;
# what clients put in it never is.
uploads/*
!uploads/.htaccess

# Isolated Harbcoin demo state. The test app code is versioned; prices changed
# from its admin screen are runtime data and never belong in Git.
test/data/*
!test/data/.htaccess
*.zip

# local screenshot/verification scratch (root only — tests/ has its own
# blank.html and publishes screenshots as a CI artifact)
/blank.html
*.png
